# Git Commit Author

When creating git commits in this project, author them as **tmwclaxton** whenever that identity is available.

## How to detect availability

Prefer this identity when any of the following is true:

1. `gh api user --jq .login` returns `tmwclaxton`
2. The remote is under `github.com/tmwclaxton/` (e.g. `origin` fetch/push URL)
3. The user asks to commit/push as tmwclaxton

If none of those apply, fall back to the repository's existing git author / user rules and do not invent an identity.

## Author to use

```text
tmwclaxton <57643714+tmwclaxton@users.noreply.github.com>
```

## How to apply

- On `git commit`, pass the author explicitly:

```bash
git commit --author="tmwclaxton <57643714+tmwclaxton@users.noreply.github.com>" -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Commit message here.

EOF
)"
```

- Do **not** run `git config` to change global or local `user.name` / `user.email`.
- If a commit was just created in this conversation with the wrong author and has not been pushed, amend with `--author=...` (only when amend rules allow).
- If it was already pushed and the user wants the author fixed, ask before force-pushing; on `main`/`master` only force-push when the user explicitly approves.

## Pushing

Push to the `tmwclaxton` remote/repo when that is the project remote. Do not change remotes unless the user asks.
